{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.PionHalfFigureEight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.PionHalfFigureEight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.half_41_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.half_41_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pion-half-figure-eight.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pion_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pion_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pion-half-figure-eight.lean#L46-L48","doc":"Both the pion and σ₁σ₂⁻¹ have determinant +1 on any 2-dim\nrepresentation (product of an even number of det=-1 generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_is_square_of_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_is_square_of_half","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pion-half-figure-eight.lean#L41-L44","doc":"The figure-eight is the square of the half-rotation.\nIf M has eigenvalue e^{iθ}, then M² has eigenvalue e^{2iθ}.\ndet(M²) = det(M)² = 1² = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pion_eq_half_figure_eight_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pion_eq_half_figure_eight_phase","kind":"theorem","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pion-half-figure-eight.lean#L23-L39","doc":"The pion and half-4₁ share the same characteristic polynomial\non V_(2,1): λ² + (h²+1)λ + 1 = 0.\n\nThis follows from: both have det = 1 (even crossing count)\nand trace = -(h²+1) on V_(2,1).\n\nTwo matrices with the same det and trace have the same\neigenvalues (characteristic polynomial is determined by\ntrace and determinant for 2×2 matrices). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:pion-half-figure-eight","label":"prop:pion-half-figure-eight","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/pion-half-figure-eight.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}